eaving IIIII),\n113:    it will be scheduled as TTTT in one step and IIIIIIIIII in the next.\"\"\"\n114:\n115:    # scheduler class or path. \"vllm.v1.core.sched.scheduler.Scheduler\"\n116:    # (default) or \"mod.custom_class\".\n117:    scheduler_cls: str | type[object] | None = None\n118:    \"\"\"The scheduler class to use. \"vllm.v1.core.sched.scheduler.Scheduler\" is\n119:    the default scheduler. Can be a class directly or the path to a class of\n120:    form \"mod.custom_class\".\"\"\"\n121:\n122:    disable_hybrid_kv_cache_manager: bool | None = None\n123:    \"\"\"If set to True, KV cache manager will allocate the same size of KV cache\n124:    for all attention layers even if there are multiple type of attention layers\n125:    like full attention and sliding window attention.\n126:    If set to None, the default value will be determined based on the environment\n127:    and starting configuration.\n128:    \"\"\"\n129:\n130:    scheduler_reserve_full_isl: bool = True\n131:    \"\"\"If True, the scheduler checks whether the full input sequence length\n132:    fits in the KV cache before admitting a new request, rather than only\n133:    checking the first chunk. Prevents over-admission and KV cache thrashing\n134:    with chunked prefill.\"\"\"\n135:\n136:    watermark: float = Field(default=0.0, ge=0.0, lt=1.0)\n137:    \"\"\"Fraction of total KV cache blocks to keep free (the watermark) when\n138:    admitting waiting or preempted requests into the running queue. This headroom\n139:    helps avoid frequent KV cache eviction and the resulting repeated preemption\n140:    of requests when GPU memory is scarce. Must be in the range [0.0, 1.0); 0.0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
