ing each token immediately,\n156:    while a larger value (e.g., 10) reduces host overhead and may increase throughput\n157:    by batching multiple tokens before sending.\"\"\"\n158:\n159:    @staticmethod\n160:    def default_factory(**kwargs):\n161:        \"\"\"\n162:        Factory method to create `SchedulerConfig` with default values for `InitVar`s.\n163:        \"\"\"\n164:        if \"max_model_len\" not in kwargs:\n165:            kwargs[\"max_model_len\"] = 8192\n166:        if \"is_encoder_decoder\" not in kwargs:\n167:            kwargs[\"is_encoder_decoder\"] = False\n168:        return SchedulerConfig(**kwargs)\n169:\n170:    def get_scheduler_cls(self) -> type[\"SchedulerInterface\"]:\n171:        if self.scheduler_cls is None:\n172:            if self.async_scheduling:\n173:                from vllm.v1.core.sched.async_scheduler import AsyncScheduler\n174:\n175:                return AsyncScheduler\n176:            from vllm.v1.core.sched.scheduler import Scheduler\n177:\n178:            return Scheduler\n179:\n180:        # The first half of this warning can be removed once the Scheduler interface is\n181:        # finalized and we can maintain support for scheduler classes that implement it\n182:        logger.warning_once(\n183:            \"Using custom scheduler class %s. This scheduler interface is not public \"\n184:            \"and compatibility may not be maintained. If you have subclassed Scheduler \"\n185:            \"instead of AsyncScheduler, you will see degraded performance due to async \"\n186:            \"scheduling being disabled.\",\n187:            self.scheduler_cls,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n188:        )\n189:        if not isinstance(self.scheduler_cls, str):\n190:            return cast(type[\"SchedulerInterface\"], self.scheduler_cls)\n191:        return resolve_obj_by_qualname(self.scheduler_cls)\n192:\n193:    def compute_hash(self) -> str:\n194:        \"\"\"\n195:        WARNING: Whenever a new field is added to this config,\n196:        ensure that it is included in the factors list if\n197:        it affects the computation graph.\n198:\n199:        Provide a hash that uniquely identifies all the configs\n200:        that affect the structure of the computation\n201:        graph from input ids/embeddings to the final hidden states,\n202:        excluding anything before input ids/embeddings and after\n203:        the final hidden states.\n204:        \"\"\"\n205:        factors: list[Any] = []\n206:\n207:        # max_num_batched_tokens need to be included in the hash due\n208:        # to two reasons:\n209:        # 1. LoRA creates static buffers based on max_num_batched_tokens.\n210:        #   The tensor sizes and strides get captured in the torch.compile\n211:        #   graph explicitly.\n212:        # 2. Inductor decides whether using 32-bit or 64-bit indexing integer\n213:        #   based on the data sizes. `max_num_batched_tokens` has an\n214:        #   impact on that. For more details, please check\n215:        #   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/29585\n216:        factors.append(self.max_num_batched_tokens)\n217:\n218:        hash_str = safe_hash(str(factors).encode(), usedforsecurity=False).hexdigest()\n219:        return hash_str\n220:\n221:    @field_validator(\"scheduler_cls\", \"async_scheduling\", mode=\"wrap\")\n222:    @classmethod\n223:    def _skip_none_validation(cls, value: Any, handler: Callable) -> Any:\n224:        \"\"\"Skip validation if the value is `None` when initialisation is delayed.\"\"\"\n225:        return None if value is None else handler(value)\n226:\n227:    def __post_init__(self, max_model_len: int, is_encoder_decoder: bool) -> None:\n228:        if is_encoder_decoder:\n229:            # Chunked prefill should be disabled for encoder-decoder models.\n230:            self.disable_chunked_mm_input = True\n231:            self.enable_chunked_prefill = False\n232:            self.long_prefill_token_threshold = 0\n233:      